1
00:00:02,380 --> 00:00:05,790
Until the very last second... 
none of us are giving up!

2
00:00:14,290 --> 00:00:19,240
THIS ONE IS MINE!

3
00:00:19,240 --> 00:00:20,950
Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow!

4
00:00:21,580 --> 00:00:22,660
Nice dive, bro!

5
00:00:22,960 --> 00:00:23,920
Defend the basket!

6
00:00:23,920 --> 00:00:24,870
Everybody go back!

7
00:00:25,250 --> 00:00:26,330
Chiaki!

8
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:29,090
He kept it in!

9
00:00:37,170 --> 00:00:38,710
Kite is totally open.

10
00:00:38,710 --> 00:00:40,180
We can score 2 points for sure.

11
00:00:40,630 --> 00:00:41,630
Do I pass?

12
00:00:42,420 --> 00:00:43,420
No.

13
00:00:44,130 --> 00:00:45,960
Our whole team is already running on empty!

14
00:00:46,380 --> 00:00:48,960
If this goes into overtime, 
then we'll lose for sure!

15
00:00:49,750 --> 00:00:51,460
The only way to win this...

16
00:00:51,880 --> 00:00:54,130
...is by going all in... from here!

17
00:00:57,790 --> 00:00:59,000
I couldn't reach it!

18
00:01:00,160 --> 00:01:01,920
Son of a bitch!

19
00:01:09,500 --> 00:01:10,630
GO IN!

20
00:01:20,210 --> 00:01:21,140
He missed!

21
00:01:21,140 --> 00:01:22,350
That damn bonehead!

22
00:01:22,580 --> 00:01:24,310
It's coming down! Run for it!

23
00:01:26,540 --> 00:01:28,750
It's not over yet! Don't give up!

24
00:01:30,440 --> 00:01:31,460
If we can get it, then...

25
00:01:36,790 --> 00:01:39,280
Time's up! The game is over!

26
00:01:50,380 --> 00:01:58,260
Back to the mirror, my dream getting 
farther with every step I take

27
00:01:58,260 --> 00:02:02,670
I want to come face-to-face with you

28
00:02:03,060 --> 00:02:09,230
Saying to the incapable version 
of myself, "never mind"

29
00:02:11,080 --> 00:02:17,170
Ahiru no Sora

30
00:02:18,750 --> 00:02:23,130
A dream slowly dismantled 
on the assembly line

31
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:26,540
(Suitable? Unsuitable? 
Pretty much impossible?)

32
00:02:26,540 --> 00:02:30,880
True feelings gone missing without a whisper

33
00:02:31,330 --> 00:02:33,880
(Not even capable of a sigh)

34
00:02:34,290 --> 00:02:40,010
None of it will end by 
placing the blame on others

35
00:02:40,180 --> 00:02:43,930
Right now, in the face of a steep slope

36
00:02:43,930 --> 00:02:48,140
My heart cries out for me to "overcome it"

37
00:02:48,140 --> 00:02:55,580
Finding excuses not to try is 
something that anybody can do

38
00:02:55,790 --> 00:03:03,130
Pushing myself to run beyond, I 
went to meet a me I've never known

39
00:03:03,420 --> 00:03:09,540
There's graffiti etched on the 
wall that says "never mind"

40
00:03:09,830 --> 00:03:13,580
Now, I bounce into tomorrow

41
00:03:20,330 --> 00:03:22,710
Time's up! The game is over!

42
00:03:22,930 --> 00:03:27,640
Kuzuryu

43
00:03:22,930 --> 00:03:27,640
Kitasumiyoshi

44
00:03:23,540 --> 00:03:25,670
With the score at 76 to 74,

45
00:03:23,830 --> 00:03:27,640
Tears

46
00:03:25,670 --> 00:03:27,640
the winner is Kitasumiyoshi High School!

47
00:03:29,580 --> 00:03:31,920
We won!

48
00:03:38,830 --> 00:03:40,330
Thanks for the game!

49
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:47,040
It's always like this...

50
00:03:47,500 --> 00:03:49,700
I just end up hurting the person I love.

51
00:03:50,080 --> 00:03:53,670
But no matter what...
my feelings for Nao will never change!

52
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:03,170
Looks like I won. It's over, Momoharu.

53
00:04:03,170 --> 00:04:05,090
Let's be clear, you didn't beat me.

54
00:04:06,130 --> 00:04:10,210
But Kuzu High did lose
and it's because I held the team back.

55
00:04:11,130 --> 00:04:12,710
I'll concede that much.

56
00:04:17,920 --> 00:04:19,540
Thank you for the game!

57
00:04:20,420 --> 00:04:21,210
Sure.

58
00:04:22,330 --> 00:04:23,540
See ya, dude.

59
00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:29,330
Thanks for the game.

60
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:31,040
Thanks...

61
00:04:34,750 --> 00:04:38,790
You made quite a big mistake
with that last three-pointer, eh?

62
00:04:38,790 --> 00:04:41,750
Yes... I think so, too.

63
00:04:42,670 --> 00:04:45,360
It was our last chance to make a comeback,

64
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:47,440
so I got scared of being blocked from behind.

65
00:04:47,670 --> 00:04:49,880
It kept me from following 
through on the shot.

66
00:04:50,040 --> 00:04:51,080
It's all because I'm still so shor-

67
00:04:51,080 --> 00:04:52,770
No, that's not what I'm talking about.

68
00:04:53,040 --> 00:04:53,920
Huh?

69
00:04:53,920 --> 00:04:56,420
I certainly agree that it 
was a poorly made shot,

70
00:04:56,710 --> 00:04:59,000
but the biggest mistake you 
made was even before that.

71
00:04:59,210 --> 00:05:00,750
Even before that?

72
00:05:00,960 --> 00:05:03,960
You hesitated whether to pass 
it or shoot it, didn't you?

73
00:05:05,630 --> 00:05:09,790
While it's true that Taro was right on your heels,
you had a whole 4 seconds.

74
00:05:10,420 --> 00:05:14,170
That's plenty of time to throw in a fake
and then take a breath for a moment.

75
00:05:15,170 --> 00:05:18,670
Or if you had kept your cool,
you might have thought about drawing a foul.

76
00:05:18,670 --> 00:05:22,460
Actually, that would have been the best option
to assure you made a comeback.

77
00:05:23,170 --> 00:05:25,920
There's no doubt, the biggest mistake you made
in that last play...

78
00:05:26,670 --> 00:05:30,890
...was not looking at the basket
the instant you got your hands on the ball.

79
00:05:31,960 --> 00:05:33,580
After #7 saved the ball,

80
00:05:33,580 --> 00:05:35,790
you should have noticed #11 ahead of you

81
00:05:35,790 --> 00:05:37,530
and felt more at ease about everything.

82
00:05:37,540 --> 00:05:39,750
Because a tie was possible, 
even in the worst-case.

83
00:05:40,540 --> 00:05:45,040
If this had happened in the first-half,
you would have gone straight for the shot.

84
00:05:45,040 --> 00:05:45,830
Am I wrong?

85
00:05:46,460 --> 00:05:50,000
Changing positions in the last quarter
ended up costing you, huh?

86
00:05:52,170 --> 00:05:53,580
Thank you very much.

87
00:05:53,580 --> 00:05:56,420
Oh, sure. Let's play again sometime soon.

88
00:05:56,420 --> 00:05:58,000
I would really enjoy it.

89
00:06:01,830 --> 00:06:07,000
In any case... out of 9 attempts
at three-pointers, he sank 7 of them.

90
00:06:07,500 --> 00:06:09,030
Even with numbers like that,

91
00:06:09,030 --> 00:06:11,890
it's not exactly surprising
that he missed the very last one.

92
00:06:12,630 --> 00:06:14,850
Only 150 centimeters tall, eh?

93
00:06:15,420 --> 00:06:17,300
If you ask me, players like him

94
00:06:17,300 --> 00:06:20,560
are going to be...
indispensable to the future of basketball.

95
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:28,460
BOYS'
BASKETBALL
TEAM

96
00:06:25,210 --> 00:06:26,710
It was a close game, guys.

97
00:06:26,710 --> 00:06:28,460
We nearly had it.

98
00:06:28,670 --> 00:06:30,380
But damn, I'm exhausted.

99
00:06:30,710 --> 00:06:33,080
Whoa, even my jersey is 
totally soaked with sweat.

100
00:06:33,380 --> 00:06:35,540
I can't get my body to move an inch...

101
00:06:35,540 --> 00:06:38,910
Well, my dudes, I'm just glad nobody died
after all the training.

102
00:06:40,380 --> 00:06:43,330
This was just a damn practice match...
and we still got our asses whooped!

103
00:06:44,630 --> 00:06:45,550
This is the worst.

104
00:06:50,960 --> 00:06:52,460
What's with him?

105
00:06:53,750 --> 00:06:54,680
Kite...

106
00:06:56,670 --> 00:06:57,390
Dammit!

107
00:06:59,600 --> 00:07:02,420
Yo, seriously? Not you too, Momoharu.

108
00:07:02,420 --> 00:07:06,040
Come on, guys. Isn't Kitasumi supposed to be
just as strong as Maru High?

109
00:07:06,040 --> 00:07:09,460
We did pretty damn well to come so far
against Kitasumi if you consider that, right?

110
00:07:09,460 --> 00:07:11,380
I mean, we only lost by 2 points!

111
00:07:11,380 --> 00:07:14,830
We've only been a team for about a month,
which means we're making good prog-

112
00:07:14,830 --> 00:07:16,580
You just don't get it.

113
00:07:16,580 --> 00:07:17,540
Huh?

114
00:07:18,290 --> 00:07:21,380
We lost by 2 points against a team
that wasn't even trying.

115
00:07:21,710 --> 00:07:22,960
What do you mean by that?

116
00:07:23,500 --> 00:07:25,420
They weren't using their best players.

117
00:07:26,670 --> 00:07:28,330
Didn't you notice?

118
00:07:28,670 --> 00:07:32,130
Kitasumi didn't have a #4 on the court,
even though that should be their captain.

119
00:07:32,130 --> 00:07:33,640
N-now that you mention it...

120
00:07:34,040 --> 00:07:37,170
And I'm betting that #10 and #14
are normally substitutes.

121
00:07:37,380 --> 00:07:39,600
It's safe to assume they have
at least 3 other players who are even better.

122
00:07:40,080 --> 00:07:43,170
On top of that, Kitasumi never made
any substitutions in this game.

123
00:07:43,880 --> 00:07:46,420
They also only used one of their timeouts
at the very beginning.

124
00:07:46,920 --> 00:07:49,330
Meanwhile, we had to use all 5 of ours.

125
00:07:49,330 --> 00:07:50,580
That's crazy...

126
00:07:50,580 --> 00:07:52,250
So, does this mean we suck...?

127
00:07:52,670 --> 00:07:55,540
That's the reality of it, 
just look at the facts.

128
00:08:05,290 --> 00:08:06,420
We lost...

129
00:08:07,130 --> 00:08:10,920
The difference between you and me is...
the fact I have wings and you don't.

130
00:08:15,040 --> 00:08:17,290
The biggest mistake you 
made in that last play...

131
00:08:17,750 --> 00:08:22,170
...was not looking at the basket
the instant you got your hands on the ball.

132
00:08:24,830 --> 00:08:26,080
We lost!

133
00:08:26,880 --> 00:08:28,290
Goddammit!

134
00:08:34,830 --> 00:08:38,410
Now's not the time... I 
should just leave him be.

135
00:08:45,830 --> 00:08:47,790
Thank you for coming today.

136
00:08:45,830 --> 00:08:49,790
Hey! Wait a sec! Please! 
Just let go of me, you guys!

137
00:08:49,790 --> 00:08:51,540
Nao! NAO!

138
00:08:51,540 --> 00:08:52,630
Sorry about this...
I'll call you!

139
00:08:52,630 --> 00:08:54,000
Such a strange feeling.

140
00:08:54,830 --> 00:08:58,960
I was only just a spectator... 
but it's still frustrating.

141
00:09:00,460 --> 00:09:01,830
This is all my fault.

142
00:09:02,420 --> 00:09:05,750
Everyone... placed their 
faith in me and my strategy.

143
00:09:06,790 --> 00:09:09,750
Hey, Nao. Don't you have a 
plan or something to help?

144
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:14,580
It was only for a second... 
but I gave up on us winning.

145
00:09:14,920 --> 00:09:17,920
And that's not the worst part,
even my game plan turned out flawed...

146
00:09:21,740 --> 00:09:24,580
Next time. You can win then.

147
00:09:25,130 --> 00:09:26,080
Right...

148
00:09:30,290 --> 00:09:31,460
I'm the worst!

149
00:09:31,840 --> 00:09:34,050
I couldn't even stay on my feet for the whole match!

150
00:09:34,050 --> 00:09:36,760
Yet I spouted all that cocky shit about winning!

151
00:09:41,130 --> 00:09:42,290
Natsume...

152
00:09:42,290 --> 00:09:43,920
So fucking pathetic!

153
00:09:51,920 --> 00:09:54,790
Nanao. Gather all of the boys together.

154
00:09:54,790 --> 00:09:55,670
Huh?

155
00:09:56,080 --> 00:09:57,830
Let's go out and have BBQ for dinner.

156
00:09:58,670 --> 00:10:00,920
But that was only if we won the match...

157
00:10:05,750 --> 00:10:08,880
I'll give you a reward in 
advance... for your next victory.

158
00:10:13,580 --> 00:10:17,670
So, to sum it up, we've got a school-wide
sports tournament coming up soon.

159
00:10:17,380 --> 00:10:20,090
SELECTING PLAYERS FOR THE
SCHOOL-WIDE SPORTS TOURNEY

160
00:10:17,670 --> 00:10:20,090
We're going to decide who will be representing
this class in each game.

161
00:10:20,090 --> 00:10:23,290
My muscles are so sore, I can hardly move...

162
00:10:21,170 --> 00:10:23,290
If you'd like to participate, 
then please raise your hand.

163
00:10:23,290 --> 00:10:25,880
We'll start with the boys. 
Who wants to play softball?

164
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:25,880
I don't feel like doing anything today...

165
00:10:25,880 --> 00:10:28,060
I just wanna go home...

166
00:10:28,250 --> 00:10:31,040
Okay. Then the next sport is... basketball.

167
00:10:31,960 --> 00:10:34,380
Um, anybody?

168
00:10:34,380 --> 00:10:37,180
Freshman are allowed to play in any
sport, even if they're on the school team.

169
00:10:37,180 --> 00:10:38,030
So please...

170
00:10:38,460 --> 00:10:39,750
Count me out.

171
00:10:39,290 --> 00:10:41,500
Madoka
So, the team doesn't have any practice today?
Then let's walk home together (^0^)

172
00:10:39,960 --> 00:10:41,500
Do we have anybody that's 
on the basketball team?

173
00:10:41,710 --> 00:10:43,960
No way, nobody wanted to join those guys.

174
00:10:43,960 --> 00:10:46,130
No kidding. They're scary as shit.

175
00:10:44,460 --> 00:10:46,410
Madoka
So, the team doesn't have any practice today?
Then let's walk home together (^0^)

176
00:10:46,580 --> 00:10:49,250
Oh, but wait, I thought 
that Kurumatani was...

177
00:10:49,250 --> 00:10:50,130
Huh?

178
00:10:51,040 --> 00:10:53,840
I'm totally in! Let's play ball!

179
00:10:53,840 --> 00:10:57,380
Come on, everybody! It'll be a ton of fun!

180
00:10:57,380 --> 00:10:58,550
Dude, calm down!

181
00:11:01,710 --> 00:11:02,750
Wait, Kurumatani!

182
00:11:02,750 --> 00:11:04,290
Oh, hey, Nanao!

183
00:11:04,500 --> 00:11:06,500
What's got you in such a rush?

184
00:11:06,830 --> 00:11:09,540
Don't tell me that you're headed 
to the gym for practice.

185
00:11:09,790 --> 00:11:12,980
I thought I was clear, everybody is ordered
to recuperate today!

186
00:11:12,980 --> 00:11:14,330
Uh, well...

187
00:11:14,330 --> 00:11:15,960
Hold it right there!

188
00:11:15,040 --> 00:11:15,960
Oh crap!

189
00:11:16,170 --> 00:11:19,400
I am NOT letting you skip out
on cleaning duty ever again!

190
00:11:19,400 --> 00:11:22,460
Sorry! But I've got something
super important to do today!

191
00:11:21,250 --> 00:11:23,040
Come back here!

192
00:11:25,290 --> 00:11:27,080
Something super important...?

193
00:11:29,920 --> 00:11:31,790
I'm sorry, but uh...

194
00:11:31,790 --> 00:11:34,580
...I don't think I'll be 
headed home anytime soon.

195
00:11:35,460 --> 00:11:36,710
Oh yeah?

196
00:11:36,710 --> 00:11:38,580
No problem, I'll just wait 
for you in my classroom.

197
00:11:39,080 --> 00:11:42,290
Jeez. This is what he gets for 
skipping out all the time.

198
00:11:47,250 --> 00:11:50,580
Will you... make sure that Sora gets this?

199
00:11:51,290 --> 00:11:54,130
I had no idea people's arms 
could even get that thin...

200
00:11:54,830 --> 00:11:56,540
It scared me to see that.

201
00:11:58,330 --> 00:12:00,290
I wonder how serious her illness is?

202
00:12:02,040 --> 00:12:06,210
Is it really okay if I hide the fact
this is a gift from his mother?

203
00:12:21,670 --> 00:12:24,130
Crap! It's been 30 minutes already!

204
00:12:24,130 --> 00:12:26,470
Madoka might have gone home by now!

205
00:12:28,830 --> 00:12:32,750
I'm gonna have to find a new way
to escape from our class rep...

206
00:12:33,210 --> 00:12:35,830
I'd like to talk to you 
for a sec. Do you mind?

207
00:12:38,540 --> 00:12:41,330
Look, I was just wondering
if you'd go out with me sometime...

208
00:12:43,080 --> 00:12:46,710
Ever since we met last year... 
I've been totally into you.

209
00:12:48,290 --> 00:12:50,740
Oh... um, well...

210
00:12:50,920 --> 00:12:53,710
Actually... I have feelings for someone else.

211
00:12:56,960 --> 00:12:58,080
I'm sorry.

212
00:13:04,960 --> 00:13:07,500
Damn... that must've hit hard.

213
00:13:08,330 --> 00:13:09,080
You sneak.

214
00:13:13,080 --> 00:13:14,380
Did you hear all that?

215
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:17,460
Hear what? I have no idea what you mean.

216
00:13:23,750 --> 00:13:26,450
I guess Madoka must get a lot 
of attention like that...

217
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:29,910
But wait, she said she 
had feelings for someone.

218
00:13:30,130 --> 00:13:31,210
Who is that?

219
00:13:31,210 --> 00:13:32,750
Maybe I should ask...

220
00:13:32,960 --> 00:13:33,670
Hey.

221
00:13:34,380 --> 00:13:36,830
Tell me, Sora, is there anybody 
you have the hots for?

222
00:13:36,830 --> 00:13:38,210
Huh? WHAT?!

223
00:13:38,210 --> 00:13:41,340
No! Um, well, there's... there's 
nobody in particular who I-

224
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:45,000
Okay, then how about you 
tell me who your type is.

225
00:13:45,170 --> 00:13:47,830
What kind of people have 
you fallen for in the past?

226
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:49,630
Wh-who I fell for in the past?

227
00:13:49,630 --> 00:13:53,040
Um, well... first, my teacher from kindergarten,

228
00:13:53,040 --> 00:13:55,720
then in 3rd grade, Micchan who was a year above me,

229
00:13:55,720 --> 00:13:58,080
then in middle school, a senpai
who was two grades above me, and...

230
00:13:58,250 --> 00:14:00,960
So basically, he likes them older.

231
00:14:00,960 --> 00:14:01,920
But...

232
00:14:02,830 --> 00:14:05,330
All of them were taller 
than I was at the time...

233
00:14:05,920 --> 00:14:10,490
...so I think that my feelings
were pretty far from actual love.

234
00:14:11,380 --> 00:14:13,710
This is especially true out on the court,

235
00:14:13,960 --> 00:14:17,460
but it's kinda painful for me 
to only be seen from above.

236
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:24,500
All right, Sora. Close your eyes for me.

237
00:14:24,500 --> 00:14:25,420
Huh?

238
00:14:25,420 --> 00:14:26,130
Just do it.

239
00:14:26,130 --> 00:14:27,840
Uh, okay!

240
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:30,750
For real?! She's just going for it?!

241
00:14:30,750 --> 00:14:32,790
Keep those eyes shut real tight, all right?

242
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:37,520
Okay! Look over this way.

243
00:14:45,210 --> 00:14:46,290
Is this better?

244
00:14:46,830 --> 00:14:49,080
U-uh, no, well...

245
00:14:49,250 --> 00:14:52,960
A gap in height isn't such a big deal,
in love or basketball.

246
00:14:53,080 --> 00:14:54,170
Trust me.

247
00:14:54,170 --> 00:14:55,420
Madoka...

248
00:14:59,250 --> 00:15:01,850
The reason I asked you to come with me today is because

249
00:15:01,850 --> 00:15:03,790
I have something to give you.

250
00:15:03,790 --> 00:15:06,880
Huh?! For me?! Are you serious?!

251
00:15:06,880 --> 00:15:08,010
Put your arm out.

252
00:15:08,250 --> 00:15:09,670
S-sure!

253
00:15:14,380 --> 00:15:19,210
Because... she's the only one who has ever
supported my passion for basketball.

254
00:15:19,500 --> 00:15:21,670
He's keeping it all a big secret from her.

255
00:15:22,290 --> 00:15:25,880
Is my son... having a good 
time playing basketball?

256
00:15:36,700 --> 00:15:37,880
Okay!

257
00:15:37,880 --> 00:15:42,000
Isn't this... the wristband
that I always see you wearing in the gym?

258
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:45,170
Consider it a good luck charm
to help you win your next game! Okay?

259
00:15:45,500 --> 00:15:47,330
You'll be playing for keeps soon.

260
00:15:47,330 --> 00:15:49,540
So I don't want you to lose, no matter what!

261
00:15:50,380 --> 00:15:52,630
Y-y-y-y-y-you can count on me!

262
00:15:52,630 --> 00:15:54,750
I'll DEFINITELY win the next one for sure!

263
00:15:54,750 --> 00:15:56,100
Great. I look forward to it.

264
00:15:56,380 --> 00:15:57,880
All right!

265
00:15:57,880 --> 00:16:00,330
Bring it on!

266
00:16:02,040 --> 00:16:06,210
I'm so sorry, Mrs. Yuka.
I can't be the one who gives it to him.

267
00:16:07,420 --> 00:16:09,330
If he ends up getting it from me, then...

268
00:16:09,880 --> 00:16:12,670
...the true meaning behind 
it will be lost for sure.

269
00:16:20,250 --> 00:16:23,210
Get ready for the
School-wide Sports Tourney
 Much excite!
No graffiti!!

270
00:16:20,250 --> 00:16:23,210
Get hype!
Today!!!
Do it!

271
00:16:20,250 --> 00:16:23,210
Defeat Class 2!!!!
Yeah!
Cute!

272
00:16:43,830 --> 00:16:45,170
Two outs!

273
00:16:45,630 --> 00:16:48,170
You survived! Way to hold it together, man!

274
00:16:48,580 --> 00:16:51,320
Hey, you guys! I think we're 
gonna need a new catcher!

275
00:16:51,920 --> 00:16:54,250
I smell another victory 
on the horizon this year.

276
00:16:54,250 --> 00:16:56,540
My popularity with the girls 
is going to skyrocket!

277
00:16:56,540 --> 00:17:00,740
Is that all you've guys got?
My class is bunch of spineless wimps.

278
00:17:02,420 --> 00:17:06,080
I'll show you how to deal
with this fool's weak-ass pitches.

279
00:17:07,250 --> 00:17:11,380
Prepare yourself, you're facing a man
who is destined for the major leagues!

280
00:17:11,670 --> 00:17:13,130
But you're on the basketball team...

281
00:17:14,500 --> 00:17:18,430
Well, Nabe. You're the first batter I've seen
with any balls today.

282
00:17:18,960 --> 00:17:22,170
If you manage to hit a homerun off of me,
then I'll give you a 1,000 funbucks.

283
00:17:22,170 --> 00:17:24,880
Don't be a cheapskate. 
Make it 5,000 funbucks.

284
00:17:24,880 --> 00:17:26,420
You're a greedy little punk.

285
00:17:26,960 --> 00:17:27,920
Fine then.

286
00:17:28,130 --> 00:17:29,460
The hell are "funbucks"?

287
00:17:29,920 --> 00:17:32,830
You know, Nabe, we've been friends
since back in Elementary.

288
00:17:33,380 --> 00:17:34,920
It's been a long road for us.

289
00:17:34,920 --> 00:17:36,830
Yeah, it sure has.

290
00:17:36,830 --> 00:17:39,530
What now? This is turning into 
some kind of soap opera...

291
00:17:40,040 --> 00:17:42,810
People would often confuse us as being twins just because

292
00:17:42,810 --> 00:17:44,810
we both grew out manly facial hair.

293
00:17:44,810 --> 00:17:47,250
Yeah, they sure did.

294
00:17:47,540 --> 00:17:48,790
Did they really though?

295
00:17:48,960 --> 00:17:49,710
But now!

296
00:17:50,040 --> 00:17:52,710
I've cast aside all the sentiment 
that I had for our past!

297
00:17:53,130 --> 00:17:54,170
Let's do this!

298
00:17:54,420 --> 00:17:55,460
Bring it!

299
00:17:55,460 --> 00:17:57,380
What the?! Why'd the 
weather suddenly change?!

300
00:18:03,040 --> 00:18:04,140
F-flames?!

301
00:18:11,880 --> 00:18:13,780
He hit it! He actual hit it!

302
00:18:15,040 --> 00:18:18,580
You're the first man to 
ever hit one of my pitches.

303
00:18:18,580 --> 00:18:22,580
I can't send Chiaki's pitches flying
with a flimsy piece of shit like this!

304
00:18:23,040 --> 00:18:25,130
Bring me a metal bat right now!

305
00:18:25,130 --> 00:18:26,830
B-but you'll die, Nabeshima...

306
00:18:26,830 --> 00:18:27,710
Shut it!

307
00:18:28,040 --> 00:18:31,920
This right here is a deathmatch
with the pride of two men at stake!

308
00:18:32,080 --> 00:18:35,670
The damn ball could gouge my heart out
and I still wouldn't go down!

309
00:18:35,670 --> 00:18:38,460
And honestly, I kind of 
want those 5,000 funbucks!

310
00:18:38,460 --> 00:18:40,300
No seriously, what are "funbucks"?

311
00:18:43,580 --> 00:18:46,930
There's no man on Earth capable 
of hitting my pitches!

312
00:18:47,420 --> 00:18:50,250
You're wrong, there is one man!

313
00:18:51,380 --> 00:18:54,360
And his name is Ryuhei Nabeshima!

314
00:18:55,380 --> 00:18:56,170
Huh...?

315
00:18:57,170 --> 00:18:59,500
He hit it right out of the 
park! It's a home run!

316
00:18:59,500 --> 00:19:00,700
Nice, Nabe!

317
00:19:00,700 --> 00:19:02,960
Class 2-1 is the winner this year!

318
00:19:02,960 --> 00:19:07,040
Thanks, dudes! Thanks for cheering me on!

319
00:19:07,040 --> 00:19:08,080
Touch.

320
00:19:08,460 --> 00:19:09,330
Huh?

321
00:19:10,750 --> 00:19:13,420
Dude, that's a different ball 
that was just lying around.

322
00:19:13,420 --> 00:19:15,710
Nope, I caught yours when no one was looking.

323
00:19:15,710 --> 00:19:17,130
That's a load of bull!

324
00:19:17,130 --> 00:19:19,080
There's no way you caught that ball!

325
00:19:19,080 --> 00:19:20,380
You all saw it go flying, right?!

326
00:19:20,750 --> 00:19:23,330
It went out of the park for sure!

327
00:19:22,250 --> 00:19:23,330
We didn't see nothing...

328
00:19:24,560 --> 00:19:26,500
Three outs! Change!

329
00:19:26,500 --> 00:19:30,770
What the hell?! Why are you asswipes
pretending you didn't see anything?!

330
00:19:33,920 --> 00:19:35,830
Do your best, Yoshihara!

331
00:19:36,330 --> 00:19:37,440
Keep it up!

332
00:19:37,790 --> 00:19:40,000
Move it, runt! Or else I'll send you flying!

333
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:41,920
Ugh, what a huge jerk...

334
00:19:42,210 --> 00:19:43,460
C'mon, pissant!

335
00:19:43,460 --> 00:19:44,620
Pass the ball here!

336
00:19:48,460 --> 00:19:49,750
Wow! He's amazing!

337
00:19:49,750 --> 00:19:51,000
So cool!

338
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:52,830
That punkass freshman!

339
00:19:52,830 --> 00:19:53,960
Let's knock him down a peg!

340
00:19:53,960 --> 00:19:55,330
Hold it, you little shit!

341
00:19:56,420 --> 00:19:58,130
Get ready for a knuckle sandwich!

342
00:20:02,540 --> 00:20:03,750
Eat shit, fool.

343
00:20:05,210 --> 00:20:06,670
Game over!

344
00:20:06,920 --> 00:20:09,730
With the score at 12 to 4, 
class 1-3 is the winner!

345
00:20:12,460 --> 00:20:14,960
Holy cow! The freshmen 
totally trashed the seniors!

346
00:20:14,960 --> 00:20:17,150
All the new students are 
pretty damn good at sports!

347
00:20:17,150 --> 00:20:19,670
Oh my gosh, isn't Natsume just the coolest?!

348
00:20:19,670 --> 00:20:21,460
Although he's still a little scary.

349
00:20:21,460 --> 00:20:24,830
He's totally awesome! Especially that move,
the double-whatever they call it!

350
00:20:24,830 --> 00:20:26,210
I've seen it in a sports manga before!

351
00:20:26,210 --> 00:20:28,040
Do you think he has a girlfriend yet?

352
00:20:28,040 --> 00:20:30,170
Oh jeez, I don't believe it...
I'm totally going to ask for his number later!

353
00:20:30,170 --> 00:20:31,380
...they're all fawning over him...

354
00:20:31,670 --> 00:20:34,230
Our class is definitely going to win in basketball.

355
00:20:34,230 --> 00:20:36,230
Nobody stands a chance against Natsume.

356
00:20:36,230 --> 00:20:37,710
Totally! It's in the bag!

357
00:20:38,170 --> 00:20:40,090
I'm not so sure it will be as simple as that.

358
00:20:40,830 --> 00:20:43,130
Since there's an amazing player 
in the class next to ours.

359
00:20:43,130 --> 00:20:44,040
An amazing player?

360
00:20:44,460 --> 00:20:46,290
Just look. Over on that court.

361
00:20:47,260 --> 00:20:49,670
Hey Kida, move further inside!

362
00:20:50,040 --> 00:20:53,710
Oh, uhhh... yeah, Kurumatani right?

363
00:20:53,710 --> 00:20:56,830
The short kid everybody was talking about.
Is he the amazing player you mean?

364
00:20:57,170 --> 00:20:59,210
Just watch. He'll definitely surprise you.

365
00:21:01,040 --> 00:21:02,170
What a move!

366
00:21:02,420 --> 00:21:04,330
Nice pass, Kurumatani!

367
00:21:04,830 --> 00:21:06,870
Huh? A pass? But why?

368
00:21:10,080 --> 00:21:12,040
So close!

369
00:21:12,040 --> 00:21:17,130
Umm... sorry, Nao. I really don't get
what's so amazing about him.

370
00:21:17,130 --> 00:21:19,000
Uh, well, that's okay.

371
00:21:19,500 --> 00:21:22,210
Maybe he's... focused solely 
on being point guard?

372
00:21:23,790 --> 00:21:26,170
At 8 points to 6, the winner is class 1-4!

373
00:21:26,500 --> 00:21:28,640
We did it!

374
00:21:29,040 --> 00:21:31,540
Wow! The freshmen managed
to survive to the next game!

375
00:21:31,540 --> 00:21:34,670
That means the next match is 
between class 1-3 and 1-4.

376
00:21:34,670 --> 00:21:36,880
The winner of that is probably 
going to go all the way.

377
00:21:37,100 --> 00:21:39,960
Oh man, Kudo! That last 
shot you made was perfect!

378
00:21:39,960 --> 00:21:41,460
Right? I'm totally awesome!

379
00:21:42,040 --> 00:21:43,670
Hey, send me some passes too!

380
00:21:43,940 --> 00:21:45,400
Sure, leave it to me!

381
00:21:46,130 --> 00:21:50,130
We wouldn't have lost if you'd made solid passes
like that to me during OUR game.

382
00:21:50,290 --> 00:21:50,960
Huh?

383
00:21:52,330 --> 00:21:53,960
I have no plans to lose again,

384
00:21:53,960 --> 00:21:57,040
no matter what team I have to go up against from now on.

385
00:21:57,580 --> 00:21:59,670
That also includes you, shrimp.

386
00:22:12,930 --> 00:22:17,880
Even if things aren't going well on my own

387
00:22:18,420 --> 00:22:22,080
There's a simple way to turn it all around

388
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:29,040
A light falls down on an 
exit previously unseen

389
00:22:29,500 --> 00:22:33,210
That's where the path to tomorrow lies

390
00:22:33,830 --> 00:22:39,920
I was never really alone to begin with

391
00:22:39,920 --> 00:22:45,080
You were in the scenery reflected in my eyes

392
00:22:45,250 --> 00:22:51,580
I can go anywhere so long as you stay there

393
00:22:51,580 --> 00:22:56,460
There are no such things as limits

394
00:22:56,460 --> 00:23:01,630
Just having you by my side makes me stronger

395
00:23:01,830 --> 00:23:08,710
We'll pick ourselves up as 
often as needed and keep moving

396
00:23:08,830 --> 00:23:16,750
Oh oh oh, oh oh oh, oh oh oh,

397
00:23:16,750 --> 00:23:19,710
Until the very last second

398
00:23:19,920 --> 00:23:22,540
Don't give up and keep fighting

399
00:23:22,540 --> 00:23:29,630
A shining light is undoubtedly 
waiting for us down this path

400
00:23:30,880 --> 00:23:35,390
Ahiru no Sora
Next Time: The Last Piece

401
00:23:31,630 --> 00:23:34,130
Next time: "The Last Piece."

